  "recipe_text": "Recipe: Curried Orzo Salad\nYield: 6\nPrep time: 15m\nCook time: 15m\nTotal time: 30m\n\nIngredients:\n  - 2 cups uncooked orzo (I buy DeLallo brand)\n  - 2 cups Rotisserie chicken (chopped (optional))\n  - ½ cup golden raisins (or regular)\n  - ½ cup slivered almonds toasted\n  - ¾ cup red onion (diced)\n  - 2 cups Granny Smith apples (diced (unpeeled))\n  - 1 cup red grapes (sliced in half)\n  - Fresh basil, chopped (cut in ribbons (leave some for garnish))\n  - ½ cup mayonnaise\n  - ½ cup light sour cream\n  - ¼ cup lemon juice\n  - 2 tsp salt\n  - 1 tsp curry powder\n  - ¼ cup white wine vinegar\n  - ¼ cup sugar\n  - ½ tsp turmeric\n  - ½ tsp freshly ground black pepper\n  - ¼ tsp cayenne pepper\n\nInstructions:\n  1. Cook orzo according to package directions.\n  2. Combine all dressing ingredients (mayonnaise through the cayenne pepper), and mix well.\n  3. Pour dressing over warm orzo, then add chicken (optional), raisins, almonds, onions, apples, and grapes.\n  4. Mix thoroughly, then refrigerate overnight; serve!\n  5. Garnish with fresh basil right before serving!",
